From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CMakeLists: do not mix plain and keyword
 target_link_libraries

  CMake Error at CMakeLists.txt:144 (target_link_libraries):
    The plain signature for target_link_libraries has already been used with
    the target "LunaSysService".  All uses of target_link_libraries with a
    target must be either all-keyword or all-plain.

Line 126 links the bulk of the libraries with the plain signature, then the
Qt6 block uses the keyword form. CMake has long warned about mixing the two
for one target; CMake 4 rejects it.

Made the Qt6 call plain to match, which is the smaller change. LunaSysService
is an executable, so PRIVATE versus plain has no practical consequence -
nothing links against it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -141,7 +141,7 @@
                       )
 
 if (Qt6_FOUND)
-    target_link_libraries(LunaSysService PRIVATE Qt::Core Qt::Gui)
+    target_link_libraries(LunaSysService Qt::Core Qt::Gui)
 endif()
 
 webos_build_system_bus_files()
